  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and Lean-correspondence
  review is pending. Source revision inspected:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope and conclusion><label|scope-and-conclusion>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-construction.tex>. It
  follows the producer actually used by the public construction and derives
  the uniform centered root-power estimate conditionally from the paid
  single-source route. The upstream uniform receipt production is stated as a
  hypothesis wherever the producer chain forwards rather than derives a
  required bound. Its key finite-volume step is the exact marked-copy
  estimate corresponding to the source occurrence bound followed by the
  centered root-test estimate. It then uses the opened-depth schedule, the
  vacuum treasury estimate, and the I04 factorial-column width bound to
  obtain the desired power of the lattice spacing. It does not use the
  alternate multisource <verbatim|Offer>/<verbatim|Thick> path.

  The proof's root-step prose is a mathematical compression of the proved
  finite-census estimate; the table below records its precise assumptions and
  source derivation. This unit remains a draft until independent review
  confirms the compression preserves every hypothesis and quantifier.

  <section|Public theorem and actual producer
  chain><label|public-theorem-and-actual-producer-chain>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Prose
  assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned source declarations and
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence / proof content>>>|<row|<cell|Public
  theorem selects one history>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.existence>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Nonperturbative/Headlines.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|existence>
  chooses <verbatim|YM.Independent.fundedRun>, then constructs the public
  continuum specification for that selected family's
  path.>>|<row|<cell|Funded run and same-history
  data>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.fundedRun>,
  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>>|<cell|Selects one run,
  campaign, and pillars with funded extraction and
  <verbatim|ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.Attached>; it does not reselect a
  family for the centered bound.>>|<row|<cell|The run's centered control is
  produced by the actual <verbatim|ahead>
  path>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.ahead>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Unlatched.rampant>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>, <verbatim|Forge.lean>,
  <verbatim|Unlatch.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Run.again> calls <verbatim|ahead>;
  <verbatim|ahead> extracts reception from the paid unlatched history;
  <verbatim|rampant> constructs the <verbatim|Chateau>/reception package.
  <verbatim|Ahead> includes the same-history strong completion and run
  data.>>|<row|<cell|Paid receipt bundle and its
  producers>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.hearthstone>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.nectar>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.fireplace>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Hearth.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gist.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fire.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|nectar> constructs
  the exact Geyser package: the escape receipt supplies Moonlit bounds; the
  purchased schedule supplies room cost, bank, and monotone radii; the
  evaporation estimate supplies the Brine inequalities; the same-history
  residence and camera data supply heights, cell occupancy/cost controls, and
  stencil locality; terminal Freight supplies the birth polynomial and
  Fourier identity. <verbatim|hearthstone> forms Scrim using this Geyser data
  and the adjacent-scale receipts, forms Fridge using the Wilson-family
  representation and birth control, then invokes <verbatim|fireplace>.
  <verbatim|fireplace> uses the section portfolios and Mark price data to
  construct Hearthside calibration and presentation receipts. These are
  actual producers in the public chain, not assumptions added to
  <verbatim|gardena>.>>|<row|<cell|Centered root-power
  producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.gardena>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gardens.lean>>|<cell|The actual caller takes
  gauge simplicity and the selected history's factorial paid-column
  condition, then proves <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Wcmain>. It obtains a
  uniform grade/radius coefficient bound by compactness of the
  finite-dimensional label ball, chooses the tabs-opened scale, sums the
  finite initial-scale costs into one constant, and applies the root estimate
  at each depth.>>|<row|<cell|Single-source served-slab
  producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.desal>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.sweet>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.sentry>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.pollinate>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Paddle.lean>,
  <verbatim|Velvet.lean>, <verbatim|ChaletS.lean>,
  <verbatim|SpringT.lean>>|<cell|The manuscript proves that the scale-growth
  march transports the occupancy fiber upper bound to both old and embedded
  fibers at each step and propagates mode separation, then proves the source
  geometric estimate by the minimizing-cover ring traversal, bucket
  separation, and the bound $B>>|<row|<cell|Public Geyser caller and
  outstanding uniform inputs>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Geyser.at>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occurs>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Badlands.lean>,
  <verbatim|Glacier.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Geyser.at> feeds the actual
  same-history <verbatim|Freightage> music, <verbatim|Geyser.heights>,
  <verbatim|Makes>, payment and terminal birth/integrability into
  <verbatim|pollinate>; this gives <verbatim|Sung>, the
  <verbatim|Brine>/<verbatim|Moonlit>/<verbatim|Fiesta>/<verbatim|Cherry>/<verbatim|Banks>
  inputs and the terminal Fourier hook. <verbatim|occurs> then creates the
  terminal birth polynomial from the census product, proves its
  continuity/integrability, and constructs its backward <verbatim|Course>
  flow. The article's conditional theorem requires the quantitative fields
  with common bounds on each bounded label ball. The upstream route forwards
  some receipt fields at the <verbatim|Freightage>/<verbatim|Geyser>
  boundary; this draft does not yet derive every such uniform field from the
  more primitive run-selection data. That producer proof remains open and the
  centered result is not claimed unconditional on this
  evidence.>>|<row|<cell|Actual downstream
  consumer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.Ties.control>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Wcmain.projects>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extraction.CenterPort.book>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extraction/Center.lean>>|<cell|The run retains the
  centered bound. The extraction projects it to the finite-volume centered
  budgets and the expanding-period cell hypothesis used by the compactness
  chapter. The prose chapter <verbatim|centered-estimates.tex> is therefore
  downstream of this result.>>|<row|<cell|Construction of the continuation
  supplying the receipts>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.ramp>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.rampant>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.dagger>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>, <verbatim|Unlatch.lean>,
  <verbatim|Forge.lean>>|<cell|Run creation obtains a gauge-flow budget and
  initial trajectory, then <verbatim|trident>, <verbatim|currency>, the
  purchased calendar, and the wait engine construct a price-controlled
  continuation. In <verbatim|rampant>, the resource level is enlarged to
  cover shell delays; the <verbatim|hiss>/later schedule step gives the
  positive monotone delay and coupling budget; the franchise step produces
  the priced wait/trajectory record. For each later requested nested
  trajectory, accepted depth schedule, transfer data, doors, and terminal
  Freight receipt, the continuation constructs the family, its portfolios and
  service data, then invokes the receipt producers below. <verbatim|Run.ramp>
  instantiates that continuation with the same selected run's trajectory,
  accepted bounds, doors, and books, and <verbatim|ahead> applies it. This
  chain does not swap families between the receipts and centered
  estimate.>>>>>

  <section|Finite-volume root estimate correspondence><label|finite-volume-root-estimate-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declarations and paths>>|<cell|<strong|Exact
  content inspected>>>|<row|<cell|Root-test and width
  definitions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.expense>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tent>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Balloon.lean>>|<cell|The
  expense is <math|<around|(|a<rsub|m>/a<rsub|k>|)><rsup|4><math-up|treasury><around|(|k|)>+6-log
  <around|(|<math-up|plumR><around|(|d,R,k|)>|)>>. <verbatim|tent> assumes an
  opened pair of levels, a grade reference condition, a finite volume beyond
  the opened depth, and a coefficient-size bound. Its conclusion is the
  normalized centered root-test bound by the exponential of this
  expense.>>|<row|<cell|Camps, copies, and geometric
  separation>|<cell|<verbatim|Work.I03.answer>, <verbatim|Stock.census>,
  <verbatim|Stock.Tabs.opened>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tent>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I03.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Balloon.lean>,
  relevant <verbatim|YM.Cells> definitions>|<cell|The centered tiling
  enumerates its sites. I03 identifies each copied observable with the
  translated/signed-coordinate observable placed at its camp. Opened schedule
  levels supply the migration map. Distinct camp sites are separated by the
  paid room spacing. The occupancy bound controls the number of labels
  assigned to a single site; it is an upper multiplicity bound. The
  origin-centered estimate is transported to every site by
  <verbatim|Stock.translate_s>.>>|<row|<cell|Per-label local
  payment>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.plumR>, <verbatim|.stocking>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Traps.lean>>|<cell|The local ticket price is
  <math|a<rsub|k><rsup|d>> times the grade-<math|d> width. Multiplying it by
  the local observable cost is bounded by the available <verbatim|fly>
  budget; the estimate follows from the priced coordinate frame, the grade
  norm, and the definition of <verbatim|fly>.>>|<row|<cell|Served-slab
  representation and pointwise price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.Served>,
  <verbatim|.restore>, <verbatim|.steer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accent.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Newell.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Served> writes
  the density as the exponential of the scalar action times a finite
  polynomial pass of one-copy observables and local unit sources, multiplied
  by a finite field sum over disjoint box patterns with vacuum, marked, and
  forced-box sources. The unit and forced-box polynomials have marker degree
  at least two. <verbatim|Towed> supplies a coefficient-price envelope per
  support and a cover-weighted hit budget. Since each nonzero support
  contains an origin, summing the origin budgets gives a total at most
  $>>|<row|<cell|Normalization by the finite-volume
  partition>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.sail>,
  <verbatim|YM.RG.Rep.denominator>, <verbatim|YM.RG.Rep.exponent_hi/lo>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Arbol.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Vac/Shelter.lean>>|<cell|The pointwise coefficient price
  bounds the toll-weighted absolute mode. Integrating against the probability
  prior preserves the upper estimate. For the lower bound on the partition,
  the calm set restricts each oriented edge to a matrix ball of radius
  <math|\<rho\>/4>; each four-edge path then has chord at most
  <math|\<rho\>>, so flags vanish. Its prior probability is at least
  <math|<around|(|\<rho\>/16|)><rsup|4*s*d<rsub|G>>>, where
  <math|d<rsub|G>=dim<rsub|\<bbb-R\>> G.*M*a*t>, the ambient
  representation-matrix space dimension. The lower exponent estimate and this
  probability give <math|Z\<geqslant\>exp
  <around|(|<math-up|scalar>-s*<around|[|<math-up|exCost>+\<beta\><math-up|baseBudget>+<around|(|4*d<rsub|G>|)>*log
  <around|(|16/\<rho\>|)>|]>|)>>. Dividing proves the displayed integrated
  mode bound with extensive term <math|s*<around|[|2<math-up|exCost>+u<rsub|0>+\<beta\><math-up|baseBudget>+4*d<rsub|G>*log
  <around|(|16/\<rho\>|)>|]>>.>>|<row|<cell|Backward transfer and mode
  estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occurs>, <verbatim|.vista>,
  <verbatim|.punctual>, <verbatim|YM.Geyser.at>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Glacier.lean>, <verbatim|Arbol.lean>,
  <verbatim|Badlands.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|occurs> sets the terminal
  polynomial equal to the finite birth expansion of the product and uses the
  course flow to propagate it backward. The transition recurrence is checked
  at each adjacent scale; compactness and continuity give integrability of
  the terminal polynomial. <verbatim|Geyser.at> gives Served data at every
  intervening scale; the weighted payment premise converts into its march
  budget. <verbatim|punctual> produces Vault with
  <math|<around|(|x,y|)>=<around|(|3<space|0.17em><math-up|fly>,<math-up|fly>|)>>.
  At the opened depth the march equals the initial weights, the top pitch is
  the support exponent, and <verbatim|fly\<leq\>1>. <verbatim|sail> gives the
  integrated mode estimate, and <verbatim|vista> uses the RG transition
  identity to identify its mode integral with the terminal normalized Wilson
  moment. The resulting inequality is $>>|<row|<cell|Cell-count identity and
  root passage>|<cell|<verbatim|Stock.tallies>, <verbatim|Stock.spacer>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tent>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Balloon.lean>,
  cell-count dependency>|<cell|The number of scale-<math|k> cells is
  <math|M<rsub|m>*<around|(|a<rsub|m>/a<rsub|k>|)><rsup|4>>. For the full
  census and constant weight <math|P>, the mode estimate gives
  $>>|<row|<cell|Centered-cell interiority and
  tails>|<cell|<verbatim|Stock.clear_interior>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells>
  stock/tiling declarations imported by <verbatim|Gardens.lean>>|<cell|The
  <verbatim|gardena> proof filters simultaneously on the eventual condition
  <math|N\<gtr\>k> and the clear-interiority receipt at depth <math|m>. These
  tails are independent of period, label, and site. Translation covariance
  then covers all sites.>>>>>

  <section|Scale conversion and width bill><label|scale-conversion-and-width-bill>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Prose
  assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declarations and
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence / proof content>>>|<row|<cell|I04
  width charge>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.I04.columns_receipt>,
  <verbatim|.hat_receipt>, <verbatim|.answer>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.cheap>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I04.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Baskets.lean>>|<cell|With <math|c<rsub|i>>
  columns, <math|\<nu\><rsub|i>> factorial order,
  <math|F<rsub|i>=<big|sum><rsub|j\<less\>i>log c<rsub|j+1>>,
  <math|n<rsub|d>=2<space|0.17em><math-up|winter><around|(|d|)>>, and
  <math|W<rsub|i>=<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|i><rsup|-n<rsub|d>/2>/<around|(|g*c<rsub|i>*<big|prod><rsub|j\<less\>i>c<rsub|j+1>|)>>,
  the exact source identity is <math|5-log
  <around|(|W<rsub|i>/\<nu\><rsub|i>!|)>=5+log g+<around|(|n<rsub|d>/2|)>*log
  <wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|i>+log c<rsub|i>+F<rsub|i>+log \<nu\><rsub|i>!>.
  Paid factorials give <math|log \<nu\><rsub|i>!\<leqslant\>log
  c<rsub|i>\<leqslant\>F<rsub|i>>. The accumulated-column estimate
  <math|F<rsub|i>=o<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>> is proved by the
  scale-increment telescoping in the separate section
  <verbatim|ex-column-subpower>. <verbatim|hat_receipt> gives the distinct
  estimate <math|log <wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|i>=o<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>>
  directly from <math|<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|i>=<wide|\<beta\>|\<bar\>>+c<rsub|G>*\<sigma\><rsub|i>>,
  <math|c<rsub|G>\<gtr\>0>, and scale divergence. This does not use the
  actual finite-volume coefficient-running asymptotic in YM-000022; that
  estimate is unnecessary for this width step. Thus I04 <verbatim|answer>
  gives <math|5-log <around|(|W<rsub|i>/\<nu\><rsub|i>!|)>\<leqslant\>z*\<sigma\><rsub|i>/2>
  eventually. Since <math|W<rsub|i>/\<nu\><rsub|i>!\<leqslant\>W<rsub|i>>,
  absorb the extra 1 to obtain <math|6-log
  W<rsub|i>\<leqslant\>z*\<sigma\><rsub|i>>; multiplying by
  <math|a<rsub|i><rsup|d>> adds exactly <math|d*\<sigma\><rsub|i>>. This is
  <verbatim|Baskets.cheap>'s actual eventual estimate.>>|<row|<cell|Treasury
  and pay conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.coastwise>;
  <verbatim|YM.Vac.treasury_stage>; <verbatim|Stock.Tabs.pay>,
  <verbatim|.chosen>, <verbatim|.opened>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Baskets.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Vac/Treasury.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells> schedule
  declarations>|<cell|Choose <math|k<around|(|m|)>> from the tabs schedule.
  It is opened above <math|m> and tends to infinity. For chosen
  <math|z\<gtr\>0>, pay gives <math|w<rsup|4>*q<rsub|k>\<leqslant\>z*\<sigma\><rsub|k>>,
  with <math|w=a<rsub|m>/a<rsub|k>> and paid fiat
  <math|q<rsub|k>\<geqslant\>1>; treasury-stage gives
  <math|t<rsub|k>\<leqslant\>q<rsub|k>>. Since <math|w\<geqslant\>1>,
  <math|log w\<leqslant\>w<rsup|4>*q<rsub|k>>, so
  <math|\<sigma\><rsub|k>-\<sigma\><rsub|m>\<leqslant\>z*\<sigma\><rsub|k>>.
  Combine with the I04 bill and the explicit restrictions on <math|z> to
  obtain the displayed <math|<around|(|d+\<eta\>|)>*\<sigma\><rsub|m>>
  bound.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-scale constant>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.gardena>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gardens.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|gardena> sets
  <math|b<rsub|i>=exp <around|(|<math-up|expense><rsub|i>|)>/exp
  <around|(|<around|(|d+u|)>*\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>> and takes
  <math|1+<big|sum><rsub|i\<less\>k<rsub|0>>b<rsub|i>>. For
  <math|i\<less\>k<rsub|0>>, the term is included in the finite sum; for
  <math|i\<geqslant\>k<rsub|0>>, the eventual coastwise estimate bounds it by
  one. This produces a single constant valid at every depth.>>>>>

  <section|Actual route versus optional branches><label|actual-route-versus-optional-branches>

  The public <verbatim|YangMills.constructed> route reaches the centered
  estimate by <verbatim|Run.again> \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|ahead>
  \<rightarrow\> paid unlatched history \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|hearthstone>
  \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|gardena>. <verbatim|centered-estimates.tex>
  consumes this result afterward. This correspondence is a route trace, not a
  claim that the forwarded <verbatim|Geyser> fields have all been proved from
  the earliest run-selection data in this unit.

  The separately drafted <verbatim|centered-budget.tex> and
  <verbatim|centered-production.tex> follow an alternate multisource
  <verbatim|Offer>/<verbatim|Thick> route and are not called by
  <verbatim|YangMills.constructed>, <verbatim|Run.again>, or
  <verbatim|ahead>. The associated normalized overlay-density price proof is
  therefore optional for this public theorem. The I04 width calculation is
  genuinely on the public route, through <verbatim|Baskets.cheap> and
  <verbatim|gardena>, and the article reuses its exact final bound.

